            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0220" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.G1/187: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-24T22:00:00+01:00">August 24, 1943—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 24—7:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5574. Declaration on maintenance and repatriation of refugees in neutral states.
                    In replying to my note based on the Department’s 4779, August 7, 10 p.m., the
                    Foreign Office states that it has duly informed the British Ambassador in
                    Moscow. The Foreign Office further states its agreement with the changes in the
                    declaration along the lines suggested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
